<abstract>
<para>
KWeather comes from the kdetoys package of KDE 3.5 and gets the weather from Open-Meteo.
</para>
</abstract>


<keywordset>
<keyword>KDE</keyword>
<keyword>KWeather</keyword>
</keywordset>

</bookinfo>

<chapter id="introduction">
<title>Introduction</title>

<para>KWeather shows the weather in the panel: an icon and the
temperature of the place you choose.  A click opens the forecast: the
current weather, the next 12 hours and the next 7 days.  A weather
service (KWeatherService) fetches the data and offers it to other
programs through &DCOP;.</para>

<para>The weather comes from <ulink
url="https://open-meteo.com/">Open-Meteo</ulink>, which needs no
account.  Only the coordinates of the chosen place and the name of the
forecast model are sent to it; the name typed in the place search is
sent to its geocoding service.  The data of Open-Meteo is under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence.</para>
</chapter>

<chapter id="adding-applet">
<title>Using KWeather as a Panel Applet</title>

<para>&RMB; click on an empty space in the panel and choose
<menuchoice><guimenu>Add</guimenu><guisubmenu>Applet</guisubmenu>
<guimenuitem>Weather Report</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.  Click the icon
to choose the place: type its name, press <guibutton>Search</guibutton>
and choose it in the list.  The place is not looked up
automatically.</para>

<para>A click on the icon opens the forecast and a second click, or
<keycap>Esc</keycap>, closes it.  The &RMB; menu has <guimenuitem>Update
Now</guimenuitem> and the settings.  The weather is updated every 15
minutes.</para>
</chapter>

<chapter id="configuring-kweather">
<title>Configuring KWeather</title>

<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Location</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>The place of the weather, found by its name.  The list
shows the region, the country, the coordinates and the elevation, to
tell places of the same name apart.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Model</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>The weather model of the forecast.  The default is the
high resolution model of the European Centre for Medium-Range Weather
Forecasts, ECMWF IFS HRES (9 km).  ICON-EU (7 km, 5 days) is the
European model of the German weather service; the hybrid uses ICON-EU
for the current weather and the next hours and the ECMWF model for the
days.  <quote>Open-Meteo best match</quote> lets Open-Meteo choose a
model for the place.</para>
<para>Which model forecasts best depends on the place.  The script
<filename>kweather/tools/forecast-accuracy.py</filename> of the sources
compares the forecasts of the past weeks with what a weather station
near you measured.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Temperature</guilabel>, <guilabel>Wind speed</guilabel>,
<guilabel>Precipitation</guilabel>, <guilabel>Pressure</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>The units.  The defaults follow the measure system of
the regional settings (Celsius, km/h, millimeters and hectopascals for
the metric system).</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Panel Display</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Whether the panel shows only the icon, the icon and the
temperature (the default), or also the wind and the pressure, and the
color of the text if it should not be the color of the
panel.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Notify me when rain is expected in the next
hour</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>A notification (by default a passive popup) when the
forecast has rain or snow for the coming hour; once for each rain
spell.  How it is shown can be changed in the &kcontrolcenter;, under
<guilabel>System Notifications</guilabel>.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>

<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Log the weather to a file</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Appends the current weather to a file at each update,
in comma separated values: the date, the wind, the temperature, the
pressure, the cloud cover, an empty field (the visibility of the old
METAR reports) and the weather.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</chapter>

<chapter id="kweather-interfaces">
<title>The Weather Service</title>

<para>KWeatherService is started when needed and answers &DCOP; calls,
for example:</para>

<screen><userinput><command>dcop</command> KWeatherService WeatherService temperature 44.4323,26.1063,ecmwf_ifs</userinput></screen>

<para>A location is written as
<replaceable>latitude</replaceable>,<replaceable>longitude</replaceable>,<replaceable>model</replaceable>.
Besides the current weather (<function>temperature</function>,
<function>wind</function>, <function>pressure</function>, ...) there are
<function>hourlyForecast</function>, <function>dailyForecast</function>
and <function>rainNextHour</function>; <filename>weatherservice.h</filename>
describes them.</para>
</chapter>

